The core concept students needed to understand

A core concept that students should understand is that
AI is not 100% accurate, thus we should always validate its 
result before using its code. 

Where students are most likely to struggle

I struggled to add an agent as I was using Claude AI. The instructions
given were for co pilot. However, I was able to figure it out. 

Where AI was helpful vs misleading

AI was helping in creating the UML diagram. However, when asking
it to change certain aspects of the diagram, it misunderstood and 
would suggest the wrong edits. 

One way they would guide a student without giving the answer

I will suggest them to ask the chat bot for the answer and kind of help
them to create a prompt that will help them to get the answer from the AI. 